Its fields are:

=over

=item prefix

A prefix is a contiguous number range for a block of E.164 numbers that
includes the E.164 assigned country code. For example, a North American
Numbering Plan prefix like C<+1510720> written like C<+1(510) 720> matches all
numbers inclusive from C<+1(510) 720-0000> to C<+1(510) 720-9999>.

